  "notes": [
    "Recorded by W1 follow-up 1 (task_label W1-followup-1); the task field is left out because run@1 accepts only W<n>-S<nn> or W<n>-T<nn> there.",
    "pglite-run.mjs (the recorder's) opens a fresh in-memory PGlite from the copy W0-S08 installed under scripts/spikes/W0-S08/node_modules, reads version(), and runs the file: mode whole is one db.exec of the whole cell, which is how a tab cell runs several statements; mode split runs one db.query per statement. Its log prints, per statement, the column names, the rows and a row count, or affectedRows for a statement without rows (PGlite's own count); environment.sql_errors is 0 when no statement raised. The process exit code is exit_code.",
    "values.pglite.handle_results are the two results of handle('k1', 'i1', 80) in order, and values.pglite.captures the final count(*) of captures; values.postgresql the same on PostgreSQL 18.6. A re-run after a dropped COMMIT is the second call: the key row committed with the capture, so the handler answers \"duplicate: already applied\". values.*.uuidv7_version is uuid_extract_version(uuidv7()), and minted_key_version that of a key defaulted to uuidv7() in an intents table.",
    "Each PostgreSQL configuration ran in its own fresh server: docker run -d of postgres:18@sha256:74935e72241653ca55e0414067e6d8763aceb8a810eb51b452253ec3dcfc4336 with --network none, --memory=6g and trust authentication, the work directory mounted read-only at /q; the recorder waited until docker logs showed \"PostgreSQL init process complete\" and \"database system is ready to accept connections\" twice and pg_isready exited 0 (at most 120 polls, 0.5 s apart), then ran psql through docker exec and sh with stdout and stderr merged by 2>&1, so the log is in the order psql wrote it, and removed the container. argv lists the commands in order (start, prelude when there is one, psql, removal); started_at, duration_s and exit_code are the psql command's. psql ran with -X and -v VERBOSITY=verbose, so each ERROR line carries its SQLSTATE; the SQL files ran unchanged, several -f files in one psql session.",
    "Placeholder in argv: <sandbox>/work is a scratch copy of the inputs this record lists (mounted at /q for the PostgreSQL configurations).",
    "Placeholder in the committed harness: pglite-run.mjs as it ran named the PGlite module by an absolute path into the host checkout of this repository; the committed copy writes that checkout root as <sandbox>, and inputs[].sha256 and bytes are the committed copy's. The file as it ran had SHA-256 c3648a9e0e91373a344735306a4b571769b4d5acccea0aabbf00b6992237164d and 2285 bytes; the substitution is its only difference."
  ]
}
